sf-agentic-tools

This product includes software derived from SF Pi, originally developed by
Salesforce and the SF Pi contributors and distributed under Apache License 2.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/salesforce/sf-pi
Extraction base: standalone-tool-cli proposal, commit
3b204a44eababb7535da92940b7aaa9f96610125.

The extracted source and its provenance are in vendor/sf-pi and UPSTREAM.json.
The bundled tool guides and Data 360 registries are also derived from SF Pi.
The instruction-only Salesforce integrations skill adapts SF Integrate's agent
guide and README at commit 067e50fbad9d2481f5a2f50cc41d340930239061, replacing
Pi-specific workflows with existing standalone tools and host/Setup handoffs.
No executable SF Integrate implementation is included.
Changes include independent packaging, shared CLI/SDK invocation, public types,
standalone discovery, and removal of Pi-specific presentation dependencies.
Additional extraction covers Code Analyzer and AgentScript/Agentforce domain
operations, with independent state, settings, process execution, and authorization
adapters. General metadata tooling is authored for this standalone package.
The standalone output layer normalizes domain data and diagnostics, saves complete
results, and provides bounded model views and local result paging independently of Pi.
This project is independently maintained and is not an official Salesforce product.
